def get_missing_attributes(conn_header: ConnHeader, params: GetMissingAttributesParameters) -> dict:
    """
    Lists the references of placed elements to layers, fills, surfaces, building materials, composites, profiles, line
    types, pen tables and zone categories that do not exist in the project, for the given types or all of them, and of
    the tool defaults, Favorites, graphic override rules, Model View Options combinations and attributes: the structured
    counterpart of the missing attributes report of Archicad's GDL palette. Every element of the floor plan and of every
    view and layout (hotlinked ones too) is checked, and so is every tool default and Favorite (with its sub-elements):
    its layer, its attribute fields and memo data as ReindexAttributes finds them, its composite or profile when its
    structure type uses one, a drawing's own pen table, and its library part parameters of attribute types; of every
    graphic override rule the line type, fill and surface it overrides with; of every Model View Options combination the
    surfaces and line types of the stair and railing schemes and the library part settings' GDL parameters of attribute
    types; of every composite the building materials of its skins and the line types of its separators, of every
    building material its cut fill and cut surface, of every surface the fill of its vectorial hatching, of every MEP
    system its fill, center line type and surfaces, and of every profile the building material, surface or fill of each
    skin and its contour, cut end and edge line types. The sources input limits the check to elements, tool defaults,
    Favorites, graphic override rules, Model View Options or attributes. Each item names the source; for an element the
    element (and the element it is part of, for a curtain wall frame, a column segment, ...) and the story or view it
    sits on, for a tool default the tool, for a Favorite its name and tool, for a graphic override rule its guid and
    name, for a Model View Options combination its guid and name (and the library part option set), for an attribute its
    type, guid and name; then the attribute type, the missing index and the field or GDL parameter that holds it. Index
    0 counts as no attribute. Read only. Available from Archicad 27.

    This response is paginated. If 'next_page_token' is returned, call archicad_call_tool again with the same arguments
    and page_token set to that token to get the next page of results.
    """
    return conn_header.core.post_tapir_command(
        command="GetMissingAttributes", parameters=params.model_dump(mode="json", by_alias=True, exclude_none=True)
    )


