def get_unused_attributes(conn_header: ConnHeader, params: GetUnusedAttributesParameters) -> dict:
    """
    Lists the unused layers, fills, surfaces, building materials, composites, profiles, line types, pen tables and zone
    categories (index, id and name), for the given types or all of them. The Archicad API has no function that tells
    which attributes are unused (only how many per type), so every reference is collected: the elements of the floor
    plan and of every view and layout (hotlinked ones too), with their library part parameters and memo data, the tool
    defaults, the Favorites, the other attributes (composites, building materials, surfaces, profiles, MEP systems) and
    the graphic override rules, the way ReindexAttributes finds them; for layers the layer of each element, tool default
    and Favorite; for composites and profiles the walls, slabs, roofs, shells, column and beam segments whose structure
    type uses them; for pen tables the current pen table and the drawings set to a pen table of their own. An attribute
    that only an unused attribute refers to counts as used. Indices typed into GDL scripts and the pen tables saved with
    views are not found. Each type also reports Archicad's own count of the attributes in use (archicadUsedCount, see
    GetUsedAttributes), so a difference shows. Read only. Available from Archicad 27.
    """
    return conn_header.core.post_tapir_command(
        command="GetUnusedAttributes", parameters=params.model_dump(mode="json", by_alias=True, exclude_none=True)
    )


