def reindex_attributes(conn_header: ConnHeader, params: ReindexAttributesParameters) -> dict:
    """
    Moves fills, line types, surfaces, building materials and zone categories to new indices, the way ReindexLayers
    moves layers. Archicad cannot renumber an attribute, so the attribute is recreated at its new index (free indices
    below it are filled with temporary attributes, which are deleted again) and every reference to the old index is
    rewritten to the new one: the fields of the elements in the floor plan and in every view and layout, the parameters
    of library part based elements, the memo data of roofs, slabs, meshes, morphs, curtain walls, beams, columns, stairs
    and interior elevations, the tool defaults, the Favorites (with their sub-elements: a curtain wall's frame and panel
    classes, a stair's structures), the other attributes that refer to it (composites, building materials, surfaces,
    profiles, MEP systems) and the graphic override rules. Only then is the old attribute deleted. The new attribute has
    a new attribute id (Archicad does not keep a given id); its name, definition and attribute folder are the old ones.
    Elements on a hidden or locked layer cannot be changed, so their layers are shown and unlocked for the move and put
    back afterwards (in the current window, as Archicad keeps these flags per window). If an element still cannot be
    changed (it is locked itself, or not reserved in Teamwork), everything is put back and that attribute is not moved.
    Elements from hotlinked modules cannot be changed and are listed; their module file has to be reindexed on its own.
    Indices typed into GDL scripts are not found, and the frame and panel classes of curtain wall Favorites and of the
    Curtain Wall tool default keep the old index (Archicad does not take them from ACAPI_Favorite_Change, so such
    Favorites are left as they are and named in the warnings). dryRun lists every reference without changing anything.
    The whole call is one undo step. Pens, layers (see ReindexLayers) and the other attribute types are not supported.
    Available from Archicad 27.
    """
    return conn_header.core.post_tapir_command(
        command="ReindexAttributes", parameters=params.model_dump(mode="json", by_alias=True, exclude_none=True)
    )


